G1303.b:
⟪δια-τίθημι⟫
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨כּרת⁩, freq. δ. διαθήκην (⁨כָּרַת בְּרִית⁩) ;] ⟪to place separately, arrange, dispose⟫. Mid, only in NT;
⟪1.⟫
	⟪(a)⟫ in general, ⟪to dispose of⟫; c. dat. pers., ⟪to assign to one⟫, ⟦Luke 22:29|Lk 22:29⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ ⟪to dispose of by a will, make a testament⟫ (in cl., δ. διαθήκην also in this sense): ⟦Hebrews 9:16|He 9:16⟧, ⟦Hebrews 9:17|17⟧ (but cf. R, mg., and v.s. διαθήκη).
⟪2.⟫ δ. διαθήκην, ⟪to make a covenant⟫ (Aristoph.): c. dat. pers., ⟦Hebrews 8:10|He 8:10⟧ (LXX); seq. πρός, c. acc pers., ⟦Acts 3:25|Ac 3:25⟧, ⟦Hebrews 10:16|He 10:16⟧ (LXX) (cf. ἀντι-διατίθημι).†

G1318.b:
⟪διδακτός⟫, -ή, -όν
(< διδάσκω), [in LXX: ⟦Isaiah 54:13|Is 54:13⟧ (⁨לִמּוּד⁩), I Mac 4:7 * ;]
⟪1.⟫ ⟪that can be taught⟫.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪taught⟫; c. gen., of source of teaching (in cl., poët. only);
⟪(a)⟫ of persons: δ. θεοῦ, ⟦John 6:45|Jo 6:45⟧ (LXX);
⟪(b)⟫ of things, λόγοις δ. πνεύματος, ⟦1 Corinthians 2:13|I Co 2:13⟧.†

G1329.b:
**† ⟪δι-ερμηνεύω⟫
[in LXX: II Mac 1:36 * ;] intensive of ἐρμηνεύω, ⟪to interpret⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪to explain, expound⟫: c. acc, ⟦Luke 24:27|Lk 24:27⟧; absol., ⟦1 Corinthians 12:30|I Co 12:30⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 14:5|14:5⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 14:13|13⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 14:27|27⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪to translate⟫: ⟦Acts 9:36|Ac 9:36⟧.†

G1330.b:
⟪δι-έρχομαι⟫
[in LXX for ⁨אבר⁩, ⁨הלךְ⁩, ⁨בּוֹא⁩, etc. ;]
⟪1.⟫ ⟪to go through, pass through⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ of things: ⟦Matthew 19:24|Mt 19:24⟧, ⟦Mark 10:25|Mk 10:25⟧, ⟦Luke 2:35|Lk 2:35⟧, al.;
⟪(b)⟫ of persons: ⟦Luke 19:4|Lk 19:4⟧; c. acc loc., ⟦Luke 19:1|Lk 19:1⟧, ⟦Hebrews 4:14|He 4:14⟧, ⟦Acts 12:10|Ac 12:10⟧; seq. διά, c. gen. loc., ⟦Matthew 12:43|Mt 12:43⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 10:1|I Co 10:1⟧; seq. εἰς, ⟦Mark 4:35|Mk 4:35⟧; ἕως, ⟦Luke 2:15|Lk 2:15⟧.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪to go about⟫: ⟦Luke 9:6|Lk 9:6⟧, ⟦Acts 20:25|Ac 20:25⟧; of a report, ⟪to spread, go abroad⟫ (Thuc.), ⟦Luke 5:15|Lk 5:15⟧.

G1340.b:
* ⟪δι-ισχυρίζομαι⟫ (T, Rec. διϊσ-), depon.;
⟪1.⟫ ⟪to lean upon⟫.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪to affirm confidently⟫: c. ptcp., ⟦Luke 22:59|Lk 22:59⟧; c. acc. et inf. (Bl., § 70, 3), ⟦Acts 12:15|Ac 12:15⟧.†

G1344.b:
⟪δικαιόω⟫, -ῶ
(< δίκαιος), [in LXX chiefly for ⁨צדק⁩ pi., hi., (1) as ⟦Ezekiel 16:51|Ez 16:51⟧, ⟦Jeremiah 3:11|Je 3:11⟧ (cf. NT usage); (2) as ⟦Deuteronomy 25:1|De 25:1⟧; ⟦Exodus 23:7|Ex 23:7⟧, ⟦Isaiah 50:8|Is 50:8⟧ ;]
⟪1.⟫ in cl.,
⟪(a)⟫ c. acc rei, ⟪to deem right⟫;
⟪(b)⟫ c. acc pers., ⟪to do one justice⟫; pass., δικαιοῦσθαι, ⟪to be treated rightly⟫, opp. to ἀδικεῖσθαι.
⟪2.⟫ In NT, as in LXX, and as usual with verbs in -όω from adjectives of moral meaning;
⟪(1)⟫ ⟪to show to be righteous⟫: ⟦Matthew 11:19|Mt 11:19⟧, ⟦Luke 7:35|Lk 7:35⟧, ⟦Romans 3:4|Ro 3:4⟧ (LXX), ⟦1 Timothy 3:16|I Ti 3:16⟧;
⟪(2)⟫ ⟪to declare, pronounce righteous⟫: ⟦Luke 7:29|Lk 7:29⟧ ⟦Luke 10:29|10:29⟧ ⟦Luke 16:15|16:15⟧ ⟦Luke 18:14|18:14⟧, ⟦Romans 2:13|Ro 2:13⟧ ⟦Romans 3:24|3:24⟧, ⟦Romans 3:26|26⟧, ⟦Romans 3:28|28⟧ ⟦Romans 4:5|4:5⟧ ⟦Romans 8:30|8:30⟧, ⟦Romans 8:33|33⟧, ⟦Titus 3:7|Tit 3:7⟧; seq. ἀπό, ⟦Matthew 11:19|Mt 11:19⟧, ⟦Luke 7:35|Lk 7:35⟧, ⟦Acts 13:39|Ac 13:39⟧, ⟦Romans 6:7|Ro 6:7⟧; ἐκ πίστεως, ⟦Romans 3:30|Ro 3:30⟧ ⟦Romans 5:1|5:1⟧, ⟦Galatians 2:16|Ga 2:16⟧ ⟦Galatians 3:8|3:8⟧, ⟦Galatians 3:24|24⟧; ἐξ ἔργων, ⟦Romans 3:20|Ro 3:20⟧ (LXX) ⟦Romans 4:2|4:2⟧, ⟦Galatians 2:16|Ga 2:16⟧, ⟦James 2:21|Ja 2:21⟧, ⟦James 2:24|24⟧, ⟦James 2:25|25⟧; ἐκ τ. λόγων, ⟦Matthew 12:37|Mt 12:37⟧; διὰ τ. πίστεως, ⟦Romans 3:30|Ro 3:30⟧; c. dat., ⟦Romans 3:24|Ro 3:24⟧, ⟦Romans 3:28|28⟧, ⟦Titus 3:7|Tit 3:7⟧; seq. ἐν, ⟦Acts 13:39|Ac 13:39⟧, ⟦Romans 3:4|Ro 3:4⟧ ⟦Romans 5:9|5:9⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 4:4|I Co 4:4⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 6:11|6:11⟧, ⟦Galatians 2:17|Ga 2:17⟧ ⟦Galatians 3:11|3:11⟧ ⟦Galatians 5:4|5:4⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 3:16|I Ti 3:16⟧ (v. Cremer, 193, 693; DB, ii, 826 ff.).†

G1345.b:
⟪δικαίωμα⟫, -τος, τ
(< δικαιόω), [in LXX most freq. for ⁨חֹק⁩, in Ez, chiefly for ⁨מִשְׁפָּט⁩, in Pss, τὰ δ., freq. for ⁨פּׅקּוּדִים⁩ ;] a concrete expression of righteousness, the expression and result of the act of δικαίωσις, "a declaration that a thing is δίκαιον, or that a person is δίκαιος," hence,
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪an ordinance⟫: δ. τ. θεοῦ, ⟦Romans 1:32|Ro 1:32⟧; τ. κυρίου, ⟦Luke 1:6|Lk 1:6⟧; τ. νόμου, ⟦Romans 2:26|Ro 2:26⟧ ⟦Romans 8:4|8:4⟧; λατρείας, ⟦Hebrews 9:1|He 9:1⟧; σαρκός, ⟦Hebrews 9:10|He 9:10⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪a sentence⟫: ⟪of acquittal⟫, ⟦Romans 5:16|Ro 5:16⟧ (also ⟦Romans 5:18|5:18⟧; ICC, in l.), or ⟪of condemnation⟫;
⟪(c)⟫ ⟪a righteous act⟫: ⟦Romans 5:18|Ro 5:18⟧ (RV), ⟦Revelation 15:4|Re 15:4⟧ ⟦Revelation 19:8|19:8⟧ (on the usage of π., v. MM, Exp., iii, xi).†

G1377.b:
⟪διώκω⟫
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨רדף⁩ ;]
⟪1.⟫ ⟪to put to flight, drive away⟫: ⟦Matthew 23:34|Mt 23:34⟧.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪to pursue⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ of persons; c. acc, without hostility, ⟪to follow after⟫: ⟦Luke 17:23|Lk 17:23⟧; with hostile purpose: ⟦Acts 26:11|Ac 26:11⟧, ⟦Revelation 12:13|Re 12:13⟧. Hence, ⟪to persecute⟫: ⟦Matthew 5:10|Mt 5:10-12⟧, ⟦Matthew 5:44|44⟧ ⟦Matthew 10:23|10:23⟧, ⟦Luke 11:49|Lk 11:49⟧ ⟦Luke 21:12|21:12⟧, ⟦John 5:16|Jo 5:16⟧ ⟦John 15:20|15:20⟧, ⟦Acts 7:52|Ac 7:52⟧ ⟦Acts 9:4|9:4⟧, ⟦Acts 9:5|5⟧ ⟦Acts 22:4|22:4⟧, ⟦Acts 22:7|7⟧, ⟦Acts 22:8|8⟧ ⟦Acts 26:14|26:14⟧, ⟦Acts 26:15|15⟧, ⟦Romans 12:14|Ro 12:14⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 4:12|I Co 4:12⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 15:9|15:9⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 4:9|II Co 4:9⟧, ⟦Galatians 1:13|Ga 1:13⟧, ⟦Galatians 1:23|23⟧ ⟦Galatians 4:29|4:29⟧ ⟦Galatians 5:11|5:11⟧ ⟦Galatians 6:12|6:12⟧, ⟦Philippians 3:6|Phl 3:6⟧, ⟦2 Timothy 3:12|II Ti 3:12⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ metaph., c. acc rei, of seeking eagerly after: ⟦Romans 9:30|Ro 9:30⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 6:11|I Ti 6:11⟧, ⟦2 Timothy 2:22|II Ti 2:22⟧; νόμον δικαιοσύνης, ⟦Romans 9:31|Ro 9:31⟧; τ. φιλοξενίαν, ⟦Romans 12:13|Ro 12:13⟧; εἰρήνην, ⟦Hebrews 12:14|He 12:14⟧, ⟦1 Peter 3:11|I Pe 3:11⟧; τὰ τῆς εἰ., ⟦Romans 14:19|Ro 14:19⟧; τ. ἀγάπην, ⟦1 Corinthians 14:1|I Co 14:1⟧; τὸ ἀγαθόν, ⟦1 Thessalonians 5:15|I Th 5:15⟧; absol., ⟪to follow on, drive⟫, or ⟪speed on⟫ (Æsch.), ⟦Philippians 3:12|Phl 3:12⟧, ⟦Philippians 3:14|14⟧.†
